    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0165" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 536.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Having received notice from Captain
                    Rodgers, of the United States steamer Iroquois, that he was off the coast of
                    France watching the confederate ships now being built at Bordeaux and Nantes,
                    and that he would seize them on their trial trips should he meet them at sea, I
                    addressed a note to M. Drouyn de l’Huys, a copy of which I herewith enclose. He
                    informed me yesterday that he had at once forwarded a copy of my note to the
                    minister of marine, and should he be informed by that minister that these
                    vessels, or either of them, had been conveyed to a neutral, he would at once
                    apprise me of the fact. The Yeddo, in the first place, and lately the Osacca,
                    being two of the four clipper ships constructed under that contract for the
                    confederates, having been delivered to Prussia, and being now under her flag,
                    would seem to increase the probabilities of the other two ships having the same
                    or a like destination.</p>
                <p>I desire, therefore, to be very careful to obtain all possible information before
                    attempting to seize these vessels.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d196-a1.xml" xpointer="d196-a1"/>
